    "reason": "The pose table carries what each render-state figure it names is built at, for the eight built at something other than zero. A pose names the figures it could not derive so that a caller modelling none of them still gets a frame vanilla draws, and that was false wherever the figure does not rest at nothing: LivingEntityRenderState builds ageScale at one and every humanoid DIVIDES an arm swing by speedValue, so the blanket zero was a collapsed subject and a NaN arm. Read off each render state's own constructor across the whole package, since javac names the leaf as the owner of an inherited read. poses byte-identical; the diagnostics log and both dumps unmoved; every sweep held its row count and its sum.",
